---
title: "4. Vocabulary and concept sets"
output: rmarkdown::html_vignette
---

<div class="learn-box">
**What you will learn**

Find meanings, look up names and define a reusable concept set.
</div>

This chapter uses the synthetic practice connection from [Getting started](book-00-start.html).
Run the sections in order in one R session. All printed results below were computed
with dsOMOP and dsOMOPClient 2.10.4. They are teaching data, not clinical findings.

## Search a name

A concept ID identifies a meaning. It is not a patient's ID. Search our synthetic
vocabulary for education:

```{r search}
hits <- ds.omop.concept.search("Education", conns = conns)
hits$pooled[c("concept_name", "domain_id", "vocabulary_id")]
```

This is public vocabulary metadata. We show names in tables throughout the book;
numeric IDs occur only in code where they specify what to select.

## Look up known answer concepts

```{r lookup}
answers <- ds.omop.concept.lookup(c(900101L, 900102L), conns = conns)
answers$pooled[c("concept_name", "domain_id")]
```

These are the possible answer meanings in our exercise. Looking them up does
not tell you how many people gave either answer.

## Include descendants deliberately

A *descendant* is a more specific meaning below a parent in a vocabulary hierarchy.
Our fixture has a small teaching hierarchy with an education-answer parent.

```{r descendants}
desc <- ds.omop.concept.descendants(900100L, include_self = FALSE, conns = conns)
desc$pooled["concept_name"]
```

Descendants come from `concept_ancestor`. Check their clinical meaning before
including them; a search result is not automatically a study definition.

## Store a set

```{r concept-set}
education_answers <- omop_concept_set(c(900101L, 900102L))
class(education_answers)
```

A *concept set* is a reusable selection of concepts. For the next chapter we need
the **question** set instead. The answer set describes values; it must not replace
the question filter in `observation_concept_id`.

```{r question-set}
education_question <- omop_concept_set(900001L)
class(education_question)
```

Both objects are local definitions. Creating one has not selected any patient rows.

## Recap

Use IDs to define selections and names to understand them. Question concepts and answer concepts play different roles.

## Try it

Look up the two cause-of-death concepts in the fixture and show only their names.

<details><summary>Solution</summary>


```{r solution}
causes <- ds.omop.concept.lookup(c(900201L, 900202L), conns = conns)
causes$pooled["concept_name"]
```

</details>
